course: dictionary
lesson: 7690
title: What is a proton?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A proton is a tiny particle inside an atom. Atoms are so small you cannot see them, but they are made of even smaller parts. Protons sit in the middle of the atom, in a part called the nucleus. «An atom is made of smaller parts: protons and neutrons in a tiny middle called the nucleus, and electrons around it.»
explain: A proton has a positive electric charge. Think of the plus sign on a battery. Every atom has protons in its nucleus, so protons are one of the most important parts of an atom.
explain: The number of protons decides what kind of element an atom is. Hydrogen has 1 proton, carbon has 6, oxygen has 8 and gold has 79. If you change the number of protons, you change the element. That is why scientists count protons so carefully.
explain: Charges can push or pull. «Electrons have a negative charge and protons a positive one; opposite charges attract, and charges that are the same push each other apart.» Protons push other protons away, but they pull electrons towards them.
fact: A proton is a tiny particle with a positive electric charge.
fact: Protons are found in the nucleus, the centre of an atom.
fact: Every atom has protons in its nucleus.
fact: The number of protons in an atom decides which element it is.
fact: Hydrogen has 1 proton, carbon has 6, oxygen has 8 and gold has 79.
exercise: «An atom is made of smaller parts: protons and neutrons in a tiny middle called the nucleus.» What is a proton? | A kind of metal | A tiny particle with a negative charge, found around the nucleus | *A tiny particle with a positive electric charge, found in the nucleus of an atom | A whole atom
exercise: Hydrogen has 1 proton and carbon has 6. How many protons does carbon have? | *6 | 1 | 79 | 8
exercise: «Electrons have a negative charge and protons a positive one.» Which particle has a positive charge? | A periodic table | A metal | Electrons | *Protons
test: «Scientists put the elements in order of how many protons their atoms have.» What are elements put in order of? | Their smell | Their colour | Alphabetical order of their names | *The number of protons in their atoms
test: «Charges that are the same push each other apart.» Two protons both have a positive charge. What happens to them? | *They push each other apart | They attract each other | They change into electrons | They join into one particle
exam: The number of protons decides which element an atom is. How many protons does hydrogen have? | 6 | 79 | 8 | *1
